# Runtime data stays out: enquiries, conversations, leads, AI drafts.
*
!.gitignore

# Except the translations, which are an ASSET, not runtime data.
#
# Every file here is a paid Sarvam translation of a fixed piece of FAQ text.
# The corpus is static, so each one is bought once and reused forever — but
# only if it survives. Left ignored, a deploy that wipes and re-uploads throws
# away the whole cache and the next visitor in Tamil starts paying for it all
# over again. 2 MB of plain text is a cheap way never to buy the same sentence
# twice.
#
# The chain has to be re-included a level at a time, because the * above
# ignores the directories too and git will not look inside an ignored one.
!cache/
cache/*
!cache/translations/
!cache/translations/**

# The index is derived from those translations and rebuilt by
# tools/faq-rebuild-index.php, so it is not worth versioning.
cache/faq-index*.json
cache/faq-corpus-*.json
cache/faq-index.gen
